# CleanPlateVA — cache-control for the public data channel, applied by the
# Workers static-assets layer (design ref docs/architecture-v4.md §9,
# D-TRANSPORT-4, CPH-M3). These rules reach only responses the assets layer
# serves — /data/* is deliberately NOT in wrangler.jsonc's run_worker_first,
# so the basic map and the shared finder (which the full tier also fetches
# from here first, by content-addressed name, R2 fallback on a miss) cost no
# Worker requests. Two rules, no overlap: a header matched twice is joined.
# The manifest is the small mutable pointer (P3: revalidate quickly); the
# finder shards are content-addressed (a name changes iff its bytes do), so
# they are cached forever.

/data/manifest.json
	Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, must-revalidate

/data/finder/*
	Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
